1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:06,970
Singapore's GST InvoiceNow requirement phases in from 1 April 2026 to 1 April 2031.

2
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:14,220
But it only covers invoices issued after you go live, so your paper archive still matters.

3
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:22,020
InvoiceNow is the e-invoicing framework from the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore, built on the Peppol network.

4
00:00:22,370 --> 00:00:28,850
It sends invoice data straight between accounting systems, starting with new voluntary GST registrants.

5
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:31,390
Retention rules do not change.

6
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:41,640
IRAS and ACRA both require accounting records, including invoices, to be kept for at least five years, and many businesses keep seven as a buffer.

7
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:43,700
A hybrid archive helps.

8
00:00:44,050 --> 00:00:55,370
Scan the paper backlog, index it by invoice number, vendor and financial year, and tie each record to its retention clock, so any invoice can be found during an audit.

9
00:00:55,870 --> 00:01:05,810
Before go-live, audit the backlog by year, scan the years still in retention first, and add retention metadata so expired records can be disposed of.

10
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:08,890
Keeping data too long is a PDPA risk too.

11
00:01:09,390 --> 00:01:14,460
Micrographics Data scans and indexes legacy invoice archives in Singapore.

12
00:01:14,810 --> 00:01:17,890
Request a quote at micrographicsdata.com.
